  </diagram>
  <diagram id="lld-4-panasonic-ac-hub-&amp;-miraie-control" name="LLD-4 Panasonic AC hub &amp; MirAIe control">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="1000" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1800" pageHeight="1120" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="t1" value='&lt;b style="font-size:19px"&gt;LLD-4 &amp;#8212; Panasonic Smart AC: telemetry, energy ledger and control&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color:#555"&gt;The AC speaks no LAN protocol. Every read and every write round-trips through the MirAIe cloud; the router is a 100% self-contained client of it.&lt;/span&gt;' style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="16" width="1400" height="56" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="acpoll" value='&lt;b&gt;ac-poller.uc  —  10 s cycle (procd S99, pure ucode)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1  MirAIe auth → access token (homeId / userId / deviceId)&lt;br&gt;2  device state → power, mode, setpoint, fan, swing, preset&lt;br&gt;3  energy, cached 15 min in /tmp/miraie-energy-cache.json:&lt;br&gt;     powerConsumption grain=Daily   over ~40 days&lt;br&gt;     powerConsumption grain=Monthly over 3 months&lt;br&gt;     ⚠ the API rejects ranges &amp;gt; 6 months&lt;br&gt;     on failure → serve cache with energy_stale: true&lt;br&gt;4  RF health, read LOCALLY not from the cloud:&lt;br&gt;     iw dev phy0-ap0 station get 98:3d:ae:55:e2:6c&lt;br&gt;     (fallback phy1-ap0) → rssi, MCS, tx/retry counters&lt;br&gt;     ⚠ retry rate needs FLOAT division in ucode&lt;br&gt;5  Open-Meteo current=pm2_5,pm10,european_aqi,us_aqi,uv_index&lt;br&gt;     ⚠ "eu_aqi" is not a valid parameter — it returns an error&lt;br&gt;6  evaluate the four models → predictions&lt;br&gt;7  write /tmp/ac-status.json' style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="100" width="600" height="400" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="models" value="&lt;b&gt;Embedded models (closed-form, no libraries)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1  Lumped R-C thermal envelope&lt;br&gt;     C = 0.55 kWh/°C , R = 4.2 °C/kW , tau = 2.31 h&lt;br&gt;     night heat ingress -0.26 kW&lt;br&gt;2  ASHRAE-55 comfort: PMV / PPD&lt;br&gt;     24.5 °C + quiet fan + Coanda louvre → PMV -0.25, PPD 6.3%&lt;br&gt;3  7-day Pune CDD cost forecast&lt;br&gt;     E = 0.790 x CDD + 0.35 kWh  (Open-Meteo driven)&lt;br&gt;4  802.11 Fresnel micro-motion radar&lt;br&gt;     link-stability index as a proxy for room disturbance&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Inverter electrical model: 47 W cruise (fan 12 + elec 5 + comp 30),&lt;br&gt;scaled by delta-T up to 728 W @55% Converti cap, 1324 W @100%." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="520" width="600" height="320" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="acapi" value='&lt;b&gt;/www/cgi-bin/ac-api  (ucode CGI)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;GET   → serve /tmp/ac-status.json&lt;br&gt;        telemetry · power_metrics · rf_health · aqi_data&lt;br&gt;        predictions · energy_stale flag&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;POST  → real device control. Stdin is read bounded by&lt;br&gt;        CONTENT_LENGTH, mapped to a MirAIe command and&lt;br&gt;        published with mosquitto_pub over TLS.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;  UI command   → MirAIe field&lt;br&gt;  power          on / off&lt;br&gt;  temp           setpoint&lt;br&gt;  mode           cool / dry / fan / auto&lt;br&gt;  fan            low / medium / high / auto   (UI "med" → medium)&lt;br&gt;  preset · converti · swing-v · swing-h · display&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;On a successful publish the handler writes an optimistic&lt;br&gt;local update into /tmp/ac-status.json so the next poll of&lt;br&gt;the UI reflects the new state immediately.' style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="700" y="100" width="620" height="400" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="mqtt" value='&lt;b&gt;MirAIe MQTT control channel&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;broker    mqtt.miraie.in:8883   (TLS)&lt;br&gt;username  homeId&lt;br&gt;password  access token&lt;br&gt;topic     &amp;lt;userId&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;homeId&amp;gt;/&amp;lt;deviceId&amp;gt;/control&lt;br&gt;payload   { "cnt":"an", "ki":1, "sid":"1", ... }&lt;br&gt;client    mosquitto_pub  (pkg mosquitto-client-ssl)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Identity:  Matter fabric 466914946561840&lt;br&gt;           space 93b6a59c3a "Master Bed Room"&lt;br&gt;           device df034e6e627b' style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="700" y="520" width="620" height="320" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="cloud" value="&lt;b&gt;MirAIe cloud&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;REST  auth, device state, powerConsumption&lt;br&gt;MQTT  control fan-out to the unit&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;⚠ Sole control path: there is no local API,&lt;br&gt;  so cloud downtime = no control, only the&lt;br&gt;  cached telemetry the dashboard already has." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1360" y="100" width="400" height="230" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="meteo" value="&lt;b&gt;Open-Meteo&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;current=pm2_5,pm10,european_aqi,&lt;br&gt;        us_aqi,uv_index&lt;br&gt;Drives outdoor AQI badges and the&lt;br&gt;CDD cost forecast." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1360" y="350" width="400" height="150" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="dev" value='&lt;b&gt;Panasonic CS/CU-NU18AKY5WX&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Wi-Fi module 98:3d:ae:55:e2:6c → 192.168.0.4&lt;br&gt;Associated to TP-Link 2.4 GHz ch 6, HT20,&lt;br&gt;MCS 7, ~-60 dBm, PMF active.&lt;br&gt;⚠ No IAQ/PM sensors — aqi_data.indoor is&lt;br&gt;  explicitly supported:false, UI renders "--".' style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#f5f5f5;strokeColor=#666666;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1360" y="520" width="400" height="180" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="ui4" value='&lt;b&gt;Front ends&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;http://192.168.0.12/ac.html   standalone&lt;br&gt;mesh.html → ❄ Panasonic Smart AC tab&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Button highlight state is derived from the&lt;br&gt;REPORTED hardware status, not from the last&lt;br&gt;click — no "preview mode" fiction.' style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1360" y="720" width="400" height="170" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note4" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Footprint on the router: &amp;lt; 1.2 MB RAM, &amp;lt; 50 KB flash, ~0.1 % CPU. No laptop or hub is involved anywhere.&lt;br&gt;• Energy numbers are live cloud values. The old hardcoded 1.344 / 3.199 / 12.625 constants (a stale August MTD) are gone;&lt;br&gt;  daily_7d carries the last seven daily totals and the 6-month ledger is 596.06 kWh = Rs 4,768.50.&lt;br&gt;• rf_health was once believed broken because split(dump, /Station .../) discarded the MAC delimiter and the following&lt;br&gt;  regexes could never match — the AC had been associated the whole time. Parser bug, not a radio problem." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;dashed=1;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="920" width="1700" height="140" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2" value="HTTPS REST" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.15;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.3;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;dashed=1;strokeColor=#bf9000;fontColor=#bf9000;" edge="1" parent="1" source="acpoll" target="cloud">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e3" value="HTTPS" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.85;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;dashed=1;strokeColor=#bf9000;fontColor=#bf9000;" edge="1" parent="1" source="acpoll" target="meteo">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e4" value="" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="acpoll" target="models">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e5" value="writes /tmp/ac-status.json" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.2;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="acpoll" target="acapi">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e6" value="control" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;" edge="1" parent="1" source="acapi" target="mqtt">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e7" value="MQTT/TLS :8883" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.3;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;dashed=1;strokeColor=#bf9000;fontColor=#bf9000;" edge="1" parent="1" source="mqtt" target="cloud">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e8" value="push" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.9;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;dashed=1;strokeColor=#bf9000;fontColor=#bf9000;" edge="1" parent="1" source="cloud" target="dev">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e9" value="JSON" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.8;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.3;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="acapi" target="ui4">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
  <diagram id="lld-5-repo,-deploy-map,-api-surface-&amp;-te" name="LLD-5 Repo, deploy map, API surface &amp; test gates">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="1000" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2020" pageHeight="1300" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0"/>
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
        <mxCell id="t1" value='&lt;b style="font-size:19px"&gt;LLD-5 &amp;#8212; What lives where, how it gets there, and what gates it&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="color:#555"&gt;Deploy first, then test: running the suite before copying the file tests the router&amp;#8217;s stale prior copy and gives a false pass.&lt;/span&gt;' style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="16" width="1500" height="56" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="repo" value="&lt;b&gt;Repo  ~/project/my_wifi&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;CLAUDE.md                index (AGENTS.md / GEMINI.md symlink here)&lt;br&gt;docs/01..16-*.md         the reference, one file per section&lt;br&gt;docs/diagrams/*.drawio   this HLD + LLD set&lt;br&gt;AUDIO.md                 audio operations guide&lt;br&gt;mitv_hidden_services_and_hardware_matrix.md&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;mesh-poller.uc           mesh daemon        → /usr/bin&lt;br&gt;roam-daemon.uc           roaming watchdog   → /usr/bin&lt;br&gt;entertainment-poller.uc  A/V telemetry      → /usr/bin&lt;br&gt;ac-poller.uc             AC engine          → /usr/bin&lt;br&gt;poller-lib.uc            shared pure logic  → /usr/bin&lt;br&gt;mesh-optimizer.uc        RF planner         → /usr/bin&lt;br&gt;mesh-observer.uc         congestion watcher → /usr/bin&lt;br&gt;mobile-scheduler.uc      scheduled policy   → /usr/bin&lt;br&gt;mesh-api.uc  mitv-api.uc  firetv-api.uc  ac-api.uc&lt;br&gt;                                            → /www/cgi-bin/&amp;lt;name&amp;gt;&lt;br&gt;mesh.html  tplink_ac.html                   → /www&lt;br&gt;test-poller-lib.uc  regression-test.uc      → /usr/bin&lt;br&gt;tv-telemetry-agent/      Android companion APK (gradle)&lt;br&gt;mitv_rust_agent/         on-TV fast control agent&lt;br&gt;huawei-expect            telnet expect engine&lt;br&gt;nokia_wifi_control.js    Nokia encrypted web API client&lt;br&gt;wifi_channel_optimizer.py  spectrum planner&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;⚠ mesh-poller.sh / entertainment-poller.sh / firetv-api (bash)&lt;br&gt;  are RETIRED references. Not deployed. Do not edit." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;dashed=1;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="100" width="540" height="580" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="router" value="&lt;b&gt;TP-Link 192.168.0.12  —  on-disk layout&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;/usr/bin/&lt;br&gt;  mesh-poller.uc  roam-daemon.uc  entertainment-poller.uc&lt;br&gt;  ac-poller.uc  poller-lib.uc  mesh-optimizer.uc&lt;br&gt;  mesh-observer.uc  test-poller-lib.uc  regression-test.uc&lt;br&gt;  ac-poller.sh (legacy)  shield_remap.sh&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;/www/&lt;br&gt;  mesh.html                 multi-tab dashboard&lt;br&gt;  ac.html                   standalone AC console&lt;br&gt;  cgi-bin/mesh-api  mitv-api  firetv-api  ac-api&lt;br&gt;  cgi-bin/mesh-api.bak.20240923   (the original fake API)&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;/etc/&lt;br&gt;  init.d/mesh-poller  ac-poller  entertainment-poller&lt;br&gt;  init.d/adblock-fast · config/adblock-fast · config/dhcp&lt;br&gt;  config/wireless  (⚠ no bss_transition, ever)&lt;br&gt;  sysctl.d/99-network-optimization.conf · rc.local (RPS, IRQ)&lt;br&gt;  mesh-vendor-cache           persistent MAC → vendor&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;/tmp/   (tmpfs, regenerated)&lt;br&gt;  mesh-status.json           ~20 s&lt;br&gt;  entertainment-status.json  3 s&lt;br&gt;  ac-status.json             10 s&lt;br&gt;  mesh-history.tsv           rolling 40 samples&lt;br&gt;  dsp-auto.log               rolling 100 lines&lt;br&gt;  mesh-selfheal.log          append-only corrections&lt;br&gt;  mesh-pending-usb-deletes.txt   CGI → poller queue&lt;br&gt;  miraie-energy-cache.json   15 min TTL" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#9e9e9e;dashed=1;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="100" width="620" height="580" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="svc5" value="&lt;b&gt;procd services (all enabled at boot)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;S99mesh-poller          ucode /usr/bin/mesh-poller.uc&lt;br&gt;S99ac-poller            ucode /usr/bin/ac-poller.uc&lt;br&gt;S99entertainment-poller ucode /usr/bin/entertainment-poller.uc&lt;br&gt;adblock-fast            dnsmasq blocklist engine&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Control:&lt;br&gt;  ssh root@192.168.0.12 ’/etc/init.d/&amp;lt;svc&amp;gt; restart’&lt;br&gt;  ssh root@192.168.0.12 ’cat /tmp/mesh-status.json’&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;⚠ /etc/init.d/mesh-poller once ran /bin/sh mesh-poller.sh,&lt;br&gt;  silently violating the project’s own ucode rule for months." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1340" y="100" width="620" height="250" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="apis" value="&lt;b&gt;HTTP surface  (http://192.168.0.12)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;/mesh.html                 dashboard (all tabs)&lt;br&gt;/ac.html                   AC console&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;/cgi-bin/mesh-api?action=  status · optimize · sync_password&lt;br&gt;                           youtube_toggle · torrent_action&lt;br&gt;                           roam_status · roam_kick&lt;br&gt;                           mitv_youtube_app_status / _toggle&lt;br&gt;/cgi-bin/mitv-api?cmd=     transport · PQ · audio · scene&lt;br&gt;                           display_state · display_preset&lt;br&gt;                           surround_mode · audio_profile&lt;br&gt;                           audio_format[&amp;amp;param=hud]&lt;br&gt;/cgi-bin/firetv-api?cmd=   transport · app launcher&lt;br&gt;/cgi-bin/ac-api            GET telemetry · POST control&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Off-router: AP #2 :9091 Transmission · :8200 MiniDLNA&lt;br&gt;            Mi TV :8080 telemetry agent · :9988 Rust agent" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1340" y="370" width="620" height="310" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="tests5" value="&lt;b&gt;Test gates  (/test skill runs all three)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1  test-poller-lib.uc   pure logic, no device, no network&lt;br&gt;     ssh root@192.168.0.12 ’cd /usr/bin &amp;amp;&amp;amp; ucode test-poller-lib.uc’&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2  regression-test.uc   live smoke against the running system&lt;br&gt;     ssh root@192.168.0.12 ucode /usr/bin/regression-test.uc&lt;br&gt;     • process health + JSON schema/range validation&lt;br&gt;     • cross-checks REPORTED values against ground truth read&lt;br&gt;       straight off the device (the audio_output_type bug class)&lt;br&gt;     • fires a real injection payload at open_url (must not run;&lt;br&gt;       uses an unregistered scheme so no browser opens)&lt;br&gt;     • source-level assertions where firing would damage state&lt;br&gt;       (§3b scenes, §3f HUD, §3i picture-mode pinning)&lt;br&gt;     • TV checks gated on a live ping → SKIP, not FAIL, when off&lt;br&gt;     • §2b probes pm path FIRST: absent package = SKIP&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3  gradle test          tv-telemetry-agent JUnit on the JVM&lt;br&gt;     cd tv-telemetry-agent &amp;amp;&amp;amp; ./gradlew test&lt;br&gt;     ⚠ Green JUnit does NOT prove the APK runs: ART rejected&lt;br&gt;       Pattern.UNICODE_CHARACTER_CLASS that the JVM accepts.&lt;br&gt;       Avoid \p{...} and exotic Pattern flags entirely." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#ffe6cc;strokeColor=#d79b00;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="660" y="710" width="620" height="400" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rules5" value='&lt;b&gt;Standing rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Always .uc on the router; /bin/sh only wraps ping / adb / nc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Tests are MANDATORY after any change to entertainment-poller.uc,&lt;br&gt;  poller-lib.uc, mitv-api.uc, firetv-api.uc or tv-telemetry-agent/.&lt;br&gt;  New capability ships with a new test case in the same change.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Deploy BEFORE testing — otherwise the suite validates the&lt;br&gt;  router’s previous copy and passes for the wrong reason.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Keep /usr/bin/poller-lib.uc, test-poller-lib.uc and&lt;br&gt;  regression-test.uc in sync with the repo on every deploy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• A syntax check is not a correctness check: ucode -c happily&lt;br&gt;  accepts a dangling reference to a deleted variable, which then&lt;br&gt;  renders the literal string "null" into a live command.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Check the side-effect log (mesh-selfheal.log, dsp-auto.log)&lt;br&gt;  after deploying anything that writes to a device.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Stop mesh-poller before any manual Huawei telnet session.' style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="710" width="540" height="400" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="sec5" value="&lt;b&gt;Security posture (as built)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fixed:&lt;br&gt;  • Command injection in launch / force_stop / open_url / text&lt;br&gt;    on BOTH mitv-api and firetv-api. adb shell is a double hop:&lt;br&gt;    the local sh parses once, the device sh parses again, so a&lt;br&gt;    single layer of quoting protected nothing. escSQ() is now&lt;br&gt;    applied twice, plus a ^[A-Za-z0-9_.]+$ package whitelist.&lt;br&gt;    Verified with a live payload before and after.&lt;br&gt;  • USB delete queue takes a sanitised BASENAME only — no&lt;br&gt;    traversal, no metacharacters, and the rm runs in the&lt;br&gt;    poller’s own session, never from the CGI.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Accepted / outstanding:&lt;br&gt;  • Wi-Fi PSK is synchronized on every node.&lt;br&gt;  • Device credentials are documented in docs/02.&lt;br&gt;  • Nokia telnet/SSH are LAN-only; WAN stays Deny.&lt;br&gt;  • The dashboard has no authentication — it is reachable by&lt;br&gt;    anything on the LAN, including guest devices." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;fontSize=11;arcSize=6;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1340" y="710" width="620" height="400" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e2" value="scp / deploy_to_tplink.py" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.4;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.4;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="repo" target="router">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e3" value="executed by" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.15;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="router" target="svc5">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e4" value="served by uhttpd" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=1;exitY=0.6;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.3;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="router" target="apis">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e5" value="validated by" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="router" target="tests5">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
